.TH KHAT 1 "October 2026" "khat 0.1.0" "User commands"
.SH NAME
khat \- ख़त (letter) \- native Gmail notifications for GNOME
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B khat
[\fB\-s\fP | \fB\-\-settings\fP]
.br
.B khat
[\fB\-b\fP | \fB\-\-background\fP] [\fB\-\-foreground\fP]
.br
.B khat
[\fB\-c\fP | \fB\-\-check\-now\fP]
.br
.B khat
[\fB\-e\fP | \fB\-\-exit\fP]
.br
.B khat
[\fB\-h\fP | \fB\-\-help\fP] | [\fB\-v\fP | \fB\-\-version\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B khat
watches Gmail and raises a native GNOME desktop notification for new inbox
messages. Checks run on a quiet schedule (three hours by default,
configurable between 5 minutes and 24 hours) and read Gmail's incremental
history feed, so a manual or scheduled check surfaces fresh mail immediately
without waiting for search-index updates. Only message metadata (sender,
subject, short preview) is downloaded; bodies and attachments are never
fetched. OAuth tokens are kept in the GNOME Keyring, and the access scope is
read-only ( gmail.readonly ). khat sends no telemetry; its only network
traffic goes to Google's OAuth and Gmail endpoints.
.PP
Exactly one instance runs at a time. A later launch forwards the request to
the running instance and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \%\-\-settings
Open the settings window. This is the default when no mode is given. Closing
the window does not stop background checks; the window can be reopened with a
later launch or from a notification.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \%\-\-background
Run without a window. When started by hand the process detaches from the
terminal: a readiness check confirms the daemon took over and the prompt
returns with
.BR "khat is running in the background (PID …)" .
The systemd user unit runs
.B khat \-\-background \-\-foreground
instead (or set
.BR \%\-\-foreground
yourself to keep the process in the foreground terminal for debugging).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \%\-\-check\-now
Ask the already-running instance to check for new mail immediately and exit.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \%\-\-exit
Stop every khat process of the current user. The running instance is asked to
quit through the regular shutdown sequence (like
.B Ctrl+Q
or
.BR SIGTERM );
any process that cannot be reached through the single-instance socket is
terminated. If the instance belongs to the systemd user unit, the unit shows
as inactive afterwards and can be started again with
.BR "systemctl \-\-user start khat" .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \%\-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \%\-\-version
Print the application version and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit the application from the settings window, stopping background checks the
same way a
.B SIGTERM
does.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/khat/config.json
Accounts and notification settings (written atomically by the settings
window).
.TP
.I ~/.config/khat/oauth-client.json
Google OAuth \fIdesktop client\fP credentials; mode 0600. See
.UR https://github.com/kodejeet/khat
.UE ,
docs/google-oauth-setup.md, for how to obtain it.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/khat/state.db
SQLite state: seen message ids, per-account history cursor, timestamps. No
message content is stored.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/systemd/user/khat.service
The systemd user unit used for login autostart.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B khat
exits 1 when an option is refused or the single instance cannot be reached.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.unit (5),
.BR notify-send (1)
.PP
Documentation, installation instructions, and the source code are available
at \c
.UR https://github.com/kodejeet/khat
.UE .
